<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>AI Summer Camp - Task 4</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/task4.css">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="task-card">
            <!-- Header Section -->
            <div class="header-section">
                <a href="/lobby" class="back-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i>
                    <%= user.role === 'INSTRUCTOR' ? 'Back to Leaderboard' : 'Back to Lobby' %>
                </a>
                <a href="/logout" class="logout-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-sign-out-alt"></i>
                    Logout
                </a>
            </div>

            <div class="task-header">
                <h1 class="task-title">Step 1: Regression Challenge</h1>
                <p class="task-subtitle">Learning how AI predicts numerical values</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Introduction Section -->
            <div class="intro-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Before Classification: The Power of Numbers</h2>
                <div class="intro-content">
                    <div class="intro-text">
                        <p class="description-text">
                            Before scientists developed classification systems, they discovered that computers were exceptionally 
                            good at working with <strong>numerical data</strong>. The first breakthrough came when researchers 
                            realized AI could predict <span class="highlight">continuous numerical values</span> rather than 
                            just categories.
                        </p>
                        <p class="description-text">
                            This approach, called <strong>regression</strong>, became the foundation of modern AI. Instead of 
                            asking "What category does this belong to?", regression asks "What number should this be?" 
                            This numerical prediction capability opened the door to countless real-world applications.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Training Data Section -->
            <div class="training-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Step 1: Understand the Data and Pattern</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Analyze these house examples to discover the relationship between size and price</p>
                <div class="training-grid">
                    <div class="training-item house-a">
                        <h3 class="item-title">House A</h3>
                        <div class="house-image">
                            <i class="fas fa-home"></i>
                            <span class="house-label">1,000 sq ft</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Data Points:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Size:</strong> 1,000 sq ft</li>
                                <li><strong>Price:</strong> $300,000</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="training-item house-b">
                        <h3 class="item-title">House B</h3>
                        <div class="house-image">
                            <i class="fas fa-home"></i>
                            <span class="house-label">1,500 sq ft</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Data Points:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Size:</strong> 1,500 sq ft</li>
                                <li><strong>Price:</strong> $450,000</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="training-item house-c">
                        <h3 class="item-title">House C</h3>
                        <div class="house-image">
                            <i class="fas fa-home"></i>
                            <span class="house-label">2,000 sq ft</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <h4 class="features-title">Key Data Points:</h4>
                            <ul class="features">
                                <li><strong>Size:</strong> 2,000 sq ft</li>
                                <li><strong>Price:</strong> $600,000</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Testing Section -->
            <div class="testing-section">
                <h2 class="section-title">Step 2: Predict the Prices</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Use the pattern you discovered to predict house prices based on size</p>
                
                <div class="testing-grid">
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="house-image prediction">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                            <span class="house-label">1,250 sq ft</span>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer1" class="test-label">New House D</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Given Data:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Size: 1,250 sq ft</li>
                                <li>Price: ?</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <input type="number" id="answer1" class="answer-input" placeholder="Enter predicted price">
                    </div>
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="house-image prediction">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                            <span class="house-label">1,750 sq ft</span>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer2" class="test-label">New House E</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Given Data:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Size: 1,750 sq ft</li>
                                <li>Price: ?</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <input type="number" id="answer2" class="answer-input" placeholder="Enter predicted price">
                    </div>
                    <div class="test-item">
                        <div class="house-image prediction">
                            <i class="fas fa-question"></i>
                            <span class="house-label">800 sq ft</span>
                        </div>
                        <label for="answer3" class="test-label">New House F</label>
                        <div class="features-list">
                            <p class="observed-features"><strong>Given Data:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="feature-tags">
                                <li>Size: 800 sq ft</li>
                                <li>Price: ?</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <input type="number" id="answer3" class="answer-input" placeholder="Enter predicted price">
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="submit-section">
                    <button id="checkButton" class="submit-btn">
                        <span><%= user.role === 'INSTRUCTOR' ? 'Show Solution' : 'Check My Answers' %></span>
                        <div class="btn-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-<%= user.role === 'INSTRUCTOR' ? 'eye' : 'check' %>"></i>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                </div>
                <script> const userRole = "<%= user.role %>"; </script>
                
            </div>

            <!-- Feedback Section -->
            <div id="feedback" class="feedback-section hidden">
                <h3 class="feedback-title">Your Results</h3>
                <div id="score-display" class="score-display"></div>
                <ul id="feedback-list" class="feedback-list"></ul>
                
                <!-- Regression Plot -->
                <div class="plot-section">
                    <h4 class="plot-title">Regression Line Visualization</h4>
                    <p class="plot-subtitle">This graph shows the training data points and the linear regression line that AI learned from the data</p>
                    <div class="plot-container">
                        <canvas id="regressionChart" width="400" height="300"></canvas>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <!-- Educational Explanation -->
                <div id="explanation" class="explanation-section">
                    <h4 class="explanation-title">What Just Happened?</h4>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        You just performed <strong>regression analysis</strong>! This is one of the fundamental building blocks 
                        of artificial intelligence. Instead of sorting items into categories, regression predicts specific 
                        <span class="highlight">numerical values</span> based on patterns in data.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        The linear relationship you discovered (Price = Size × $300 per sq ft) is exactly how AI models work. 
                        They analyze training data to find mathematical patterns, then use those patterns to make predictions 
                        about new data. This is called a <strong>linear regression model</strong>.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        In real-world applications, regression powers everything from stock market predictions and weather forecasting 
                        to medical dosage calculations and autonomous vehicle speed control. Any time AI needs to predict a number 
                        rather than a category, it's using regression.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        What makes this powerful is that once the AI learns the pattern from training data, it can make predictions 
                        for any new input—even values it has never seen before. This is the foundation of how AI systems learn 
                        and generalize from examples.
                    </p>
                    <h4 class="explanation-title">Understanding the Regression Plot</h4>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        The visualization above shows exactly how AI "sees" and works with data. The <strong>blue circles</strong> 
                        represent the training data that the AI learned from. The <strong>purple line</strong> is the mathematical 
                        relationship (y = 300x) that the AI discovered by analyzing these points.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        Your <strong>gold circles</strong> show where your predictions landed, while the <strong>green triangles</strong> 
                        show the mathematically correct answers. When your predictions are close to the purple line, you're thinking 
                        like the AI model! This linear regression line allows the AI to predict prices for any house size, even ones 
                        it has never seen before.
                    </p>
                    <p class="explanation-text">
                        In real AI systems, this same process happens with much more complex data—the computer finds patterns in 
                        thousands or millions of data points and creates mathematical models to make predictions. The visualization 
                        helps us understand how AI transforms raw data into actionable insights.
                    </p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="next-section">
                    <button id="nextButton" class="next-btn">
                        <span>Continue to Next Task</span>
                        <div class="btn-icon">
                            <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

    <script src="/js/task4.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
